## LangSmith expands managed deployments inside customers’ cloud accounts

Source: LangChain — https://www.langchain.com/blog/langsmith-byoc-aws-gc-azure
Published: 2026-11-03
Channel: news

LangSmith is an agent engineering platform for debugging runs, evaluating changes and deploying agents. Its Bring Your Own Cloud offering lets LangChain operate the service while sensitive application data stays in the customer’s cloud account. The announcement expands that deployment model to Azure and Google Cloud in beta, alongside generally available AWS support.

The arrangement separates two responsibilities. LangChain operates a control plane containing authentication, organization configuration, billing metadata, hashed API keys and static interface assets. The customer owns a data plane holding traces, prompts, datasets, experiments, deployments and workspace secrets. An organization can have several data planes, separated by account and region, with workspaces assigned to each.

Teams moving from self-hosting use an open-source tool for workspace resources such as datasets, experiments and prompts. Traces, runs and feedback require a separate migration performed by LangChain; the announcement says trace migration is available on AWS. Google Cloud deployments initially use the US control plane, and Azure sandbox support remains planned. Those limits matter when assessing data boundaries and migration readiness.

Why it matters: For platform and security teams: map control-plane metadata separately from trace content, and confirm migration support for the chosen cloud.

