## LangWatch adds dataset history and pins test runs to dataset versions

Source: LangWatch · GitHub release — https://github.com/langwatch/langwatch/releases/tag/langwatch%40v3.23.0
Published: 2026-11-03
Channel: github

LangWatch is an AI observability and evaluation platform. Its release adds dataset version history with automatic saving, comparison, restoration, retention and run pinning. The linked implementation explains the problem: edits previously left teams without a way to recover earlier dataset contents or identify which rows an experiment used. A version is an immutable snapshot of the dataset’s columns and rows.

First, edits can produce an automatic saved version after activity settles. Teams can then compare a version with current contents or restore it as a new version without rewriting history. When an experiment starts, it records the dataset version it read; pinning selects a particular version instead of the latest. Agent and evaluator versioning also gain deployment labels. These changes make evaluation inputs more explicit, without independently proving complete reproducibility.

For teams collecting coding-agent activity, the release adds capture of Grok CLI sessions through native OpenTelemetry and recognizes pi as a natively instrumented agent. OpenTelemetry is a standard way to emit operational records. Separate evaluation changes expand the supported decision-model providers and make Instant Evals use the saved model and the project’s own key. These are release-note claims; the notes do not establish identical trace coverage across every supported agent.

Why it matters: For evaluation owners: verify the dataset, agent and evaluator versions associated with a run before comparing it with another result.

