## Honeycomb previews agent checks that link findings to production evidence

Source: Honeycomb — https://www.honeycomb.io/blog/honeycomb-team-agents-ai-sre-done-right
Published: 2026-11-03
Channel: news

Honeycomb is an observability platform that uses production telemetry to investigate software behavior. Its Team Agents preview describes background assistants that work on goals set by a team. One proposed goal directly concerns AI operations: compare Braintrust evaluation scores with live conversation traces after a prompt or model change.

The workflow starts with a goal and a trigger, such as a deployment, alert or schedule. The agent investigates telemetry and can use connectors based on the Model Context Protocol to access supporting information such as deployments, documentation and costs. Honeycomb says findings link to the query, trace or deployment behind them, and numerical statements distinguish measured, derived, estimated and unset values.

Teams then choose how much action to permit for each goal and tool. The described modes range from observation and recommendations to preparing changes for human approval or operating within defined boundaries. Each agent has its own identity, permissions and recorded actions. The post presents a preview with general availability planned, rather than evidence that these workflows have already improved agent quality in production.

Why it matters: For teams checking AI releases: test whether each finding reaches the underlying trace and whether action permissions match the investigation’s risk.

