## CrowdStrike plans to bring Fiddler’s agent evaluations and traces into Falcon

Source: CrowdStrike — https://www.crowdstrike.com/en-us/press-releases/crowdstrike-to-acquire-fiddler-to-deliver-agent-observability/
Published: 2026-11-03
Channel: news

Fiddler AI provides agent observability and explainability, helping teams examine agent behavior. CrowdStrike has signed a definitive agreement to acquire it and plans to offer its capabilities through the Falcon security platform. The announcement separates securing agents against attack from checking whether an agent behaved as intended while using valid credentials and approved tools.

The proposed integration starts with evaluation before deployment, checking accuracy, task completion and policy compliance across prompts, models and configurations. In production, it would trace decisions and tool calls across agent hierarchies, then look for behavioral drift, hallucinations and unintended actions. CrowdStrike also describes combining those records with identity, cloud and runtime telemetry to investigate behavior in its security context.

The source lists OpenTelemetry instrumentation and several supported agent frameworks, alongside token and spending visibility. These are the company’s planned product capabilities, not independent proof of accountability or improved safety. The acquisition remains subject to closing conditions, and Falcon Observe is described as a forthcoming offering. Teams should distinguish the signed agreement from completed ownership and from an already integrated deployment.

Why it matters: For agent-platform owners: watch how trace access, evaluation workflows and security context are integrated after closing rather than assuming immediate availability.

